      "writtenOn": "2022-03-24T22:24:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You should move the allocation of these structures into a C source file.  \n\nPutting this here will allocate storage for every C source file that includes intelrvp.h.  This definitions should also be marked `const`.\n\nI suggest intel_rvp_board_id.c.  You should also follow the Zephyr driver convention and include this definition at the top of the file:\n\n```\n#define DT_DRV_COMPAT intel_rvp_board_id\n```\n\nYou can the use the Zephyr helper macros that rely on `DT_DRV_COMPAT` to create the arrays.  Also see `GPIO_DT_SPEC_GET_BY_IDX` which is already setup to fully initialize a `gpio_dt_spec` structure.",
